  "summary": "Kewaskum Police Chief Tom Bishop said the department will not renew its Flock Safety contract after its sole ALPR camera was stolen in July and amid public pushback in nearby Washington County communities. The chief said the pause may not be permanent and he may revisit the technology later.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Kewaskum police will not renew their contract with Flock Safety, the department's police chief said, after an AI license plate-reading camera in the village was cut down and stolen earlier this year.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Police Chief Tom Bishop said that since there has been so much public pushback in Germantown, Slinger and Hartford, his team opted not to replace the stolen camera or renew their contract with Flock.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
